IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `spc-nouns`

-- State Pension Credit Act 2002 -- LAYER 1, Schedule 1 (Administration).
--
-- Schedule 1 amends Part 1 of the Administration Act and Part 1 of the Social
-- Security Act 1998 so that state pension credit is dealt with like other benefits
-- (claims, decisions, appeals), and adds one free-standing provision (Part 3). The
-- paragraphs that insert state pension credit into a list in another Act do not
-- state a rule of their own and are inert here; their effects are carried by facts
-- the encoded rules ask (that a claim has been made; that a decision is under
-- section 8, 9 or 10 of the Social Security Act 1998). Three paragraphs carry a
-- test and are encoded: paragraph 3 (the evidence a claimant may be asked for),
-- paragraph 12 (the decisions against which an appeal lies) and paragraph 13 (the
-- amount payable for part of a week).

§ `Schedule 1 -- Administration`

§§ `Part 1 -- Amendments of the Administration Act`

-- Paragraph 1 introduces the Part.
-- Paragraph 2 adds "(ab) state pension credit" to the list of benefits in section 1(4)
-- of the Administration Act, which makes entitlement depend on the making of a claim
-- (and on national insurance numbers and evidence). Its effect on a claimant is carried
-- by the input `a claim has been made and the Administration Act section 1 conditions
-- are met`, used in `s 17(1) -- entitled to state pension credit`
-- (spc-part-entitlement.l4).
-- Paragraph 3(1), (2): section 5 of the Administration Act is amended by adding
-- "(ab) state pension credit" to the list of benefits in section 5(2).
-- Not encoded, for those reasons.

-- Paragraph 3(3) inserts section 5(3A) into the Administration Act: the information or
-- evidence regulations may ask for, in connection with a claim or an award, includes
-- (for state pension credit) information or evidence as to the likelihood of future
-- changes in a person's circumstances which is needed for determining (a) whether a
-- period should be specified as an assessed income period under section 6, and (b) if
-- so, its length. The regulations themselves are not among the inputs; what the
-- paragraph settles is that evidence of that kind falls within what they may require.
-- src:397 | (3A) The references in paragraphs (h) and (hh) of subsection (1) above to information or evidence needed for the determination of a claim or of any question arising in connection with a claim or (as the case may be) for a determination whether a decision on an award should be revised or should be superseded, includes, in the case of state pension credit, a reference to information or evidence as to the likelihood of future changes in a person’s circumstances which is needed for determining—
-- src:398 | (a) whether a period should be specified as an assessed income period under section 6 of the State Pension Credit Act 2002 in relation to any decision; and
-- src:399 | (b) if so, the length of the period to be so specified.
@ref Sch 1 para 3(3) (inserting s 5(3A) of the Administration Act) (src:397-399)
GIVEN `the information or evidence concerns the likelihood of future changes in the person's circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is needed for determining whether a period should be specified as an assessed income period under section 6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is needed for determining the length of the period to be specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 3(3A) -- the information or evidence is within what the regulations may require for state pension credit` `the information or evidence concerns the likelihood of future changes in the person's circumstances` `it is needed for determining whether a period should be specified as an assessed income period under section 6` `it is needed for determining the length of the period to be specified` MEANS
        `the information or evidence concerns the likelihood of future changes in the person's circumstances`
    AND (       "(a) whether a period should be specified as an assessed income period under section 6 of the State Pension Credit Act 2002 in relation to any decision; and" ... `it is needed for determining whether a period should be specified as an assessed income period under section 6`
            OR  "(b) if so, the length of the period to be so specified." ... `it is needed for determining the length of the period to be specified` )

§§ `Part 2 -- Amendments of the Social Security Act 1998`

-- Paragraph 4 introduces the Part.
-- Paragraph 5 adds this Act to the definition of "relevant enactment" in section 2(2)
-- (use of computers). Paragraph 6 adds state pension credit to "relevant benefit" and
-- this Act to "relevant enactment" in section 8 (decisions by the Secretary of State).
-- Paragraph 7 adds this Act to the definition of "the current legislation" in section
-- 11(3) (regulations about decisions). Paragraph 8 inserts section 22(4) (suspension of
-- benefit for failure to furnish information) applying the new section 5(3A) of the
-- Administration Act. Paragraph 9 adds state pension credit to "benefit" in section
-- 27(7) (restrictions on entitlement in cases of error). Paragraph 10 adds this Act to
-- section 28(3) (correction of errors and setting aside of decisions). Paragraph 11
-- adds section 159B(1)(b) of the Administration Act (state pension credit) to the
-- decisions against which no appeal lies.
-- Each inserts a name into a list in another Act and states no test of its own; the
-- facts they bear on are asked where the encoded rules need them (a decision under
-- section 8, 9 or 10 of the Social Security Act 1998: spc-part-retirement.l4; a
-- restriction under section 27: `s 17(1) -- entitled to state pension credit`).

-- Paragraph 12 inserts paragraphs 8A to 8D into Schedule 3 to the Social Security Act
-- 1998: the decisions about an assessed income period against which an appeal lies.
-- The four are listed; a decision of any other kind is not answered by this
-- paragraph (the general right of appeal in the 1998 Act is not among the inputs), so
-- the rule says "Not covered by this encoding" for it rather than "no".
DECLARE `Decision about state pension credit` IS ONE OF
    `A decision whether to specify a period as an assessed income period under section 6`                  -- 8A
    `A decision as to the period to be so specified`                                                       -- 8B
    `A decision whether an assessed income period comes to an end by virtue of section 9(4) or (5)`        -- 8C
    `A decision as to when the assessed income period so ends`                                             -- 8D
    `A decision of another kind`

-- src:432 | In Schedule 3 (decisions against which appeal lies) after paragraph 8 insert—
-- src:433 | State pension credit
-- src:434 | 8A A decision whether to specify a period as an assessed income period under section 6 of the State Pension Credit Act 2002.
-- src:435 | 8B If so, a decision as to the period to be so specified.
-- src:436 | 8C A decision whether an assessed income period comes to an end by virtue of section 9(4) or (5) of that Act.
-- src:437 | 8D If so, a decision as to when the assessed income period so ends.
@ref Sch 1 para 12 (inserting paras 8A to 8D of Schedule 3 to the Social Security Act 1998) (src:432-437)
GIVEN decision IS A `Decision about state pension credit`
GIVETH AN Answer
`Sch 1 para 12 -- an appeal lies against` decision MEANS
    CONSIDER decision
        WHEN `A decision whether to specify a period as an assessed income period under section 6` THEN `The Act says yes`
        WHEN `A decision as to the period to be so specified` THEN `The Act says yes`
        WHEN `A decision whether an assessed income period comes to an end by virtue of section 9(4) or (5)` THEN `The Act says yes`
        WHEN `A decision as to when the assessed income period so ends` THEN `The Act says yes`
        WHEN `A decision of another kind` THEN `Not covered by this encoding`

§§ `Part 3 -- Miscellaneous and supplementary`

-- Paragraph 13: where a person is entitled to state pension credit (a) for a period of
-- less than a week which is the whole period for which it is payable, or (b) for any
-- other period of less than a week for which it is payable, the amount payable for
-- that period is such amount as may be prescribed (which may be nil: sub-paragraph
-- (2)). A period of a week or more is not touched by this paragraph, so NOTHING is
-- returned for it. A "week" is 7 days (the Act does not say; fork F-17, NOTES.md).
-- src:440 | (1) Where a person is entitled to state pension credit—
-- src:441 | (a) for a period of less than a week, which is the whole period for which state pension credit is payable, or
-- src:442 | (b) for any other period of less than a week for which it is payable,
-- src:443 | the amount payable for that period shall be such amount as may be prescribed.
-- src:444 | (2) The power conferred by sub-paragraph (1) to prescribe an amount includes power to prescribe nil as an amount.
@ref Sch 1 para 13 (src:440-444)
GIVEN `the number of days in the period for which the person is entitled` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount prescribed for a period of less than a week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 1 para 13 -- the amount payable for a period of` `the number of days in the period for which the person is entitled` `days` `given the prescribed amount` `the amount prescribed for a period of less than a week` MEANS
    IF `the number of days in the period for which the person is entitled` LESS THAN 7
    THEN JUST `the amount prescribed for a period of less than a week`
    ELSE NOTHING
